      "statement": "For the protected BLS12-381 auxiliary-powers G1 target at n=2^20, one cold run of the supplied run-gated, interleaved round-stopped paired class-walk Cheon algorithm with row-product batch rounds and table reductions (proof.md s46-s48) recovers s with probability at least 0.39 over the uniform challenge and fresh algorithm coins, conditional on H1' (two-sided prefix coverage, proof.md s45; H1 is its last case), H2-H5 in source-proof.md (H4 as per-class pair fraction 998/1000 and leaf share 193/200, checked before group work). The run first draws one fresh 64-bit coin: with probability 1-K/2^64 it stops there at charged cost 64 and fails (a closed gate is a failure, never a success); K=7202852476204064136 is the least integer with (K/2^64) lo_run>=0.39, lo_run=0.998802934325557228480247606338150492880182266878332434908126 being the lower bound of an opened run's success at the realized K = 6 N_b N_g/m >= K_T = 727/100 (proof.md s2). An opened run walks its baby and giant bases in at most 2^16 interleaved rounds, every owner record inserting into its own side's table and looking up the other's, and stops at the first round that yields a verified s. W(n) is the expected total work of this one run over that probability space, every trial, failure and closed gate included: W(n)<=2^114.609165226292 G1-reference units (C=2000) for 2^20<=n<r, namely (64+(K/2^64) E_run)/2000 with E_run=162271297721628349320552605318692337491 instructions bounding an opened run's mean work (proof.md s45). This bounds the mean, not one run: every run does at most 2^117.570097256404 units, and an opened run can cost more than W(n). It reads only A_1,A_(2^20). Challenge-independent preprocessing<2^107.1125 units, included; peak memory<2^125.0002 bytes; no advice. All failures, transfers, verification and output are charged. Nodes use the disclosed flat unsigned 64-bit address model. This is an analytic conditional bound, not a production execution. Q=247/200 and K_T are retained design values from the immediate source, not proved minima at the new prices. H1' and H2-H5 are not closed.",
